How's this for a great way to die?

In the endgame, after defeating the wizard 4 times on the way up.  Get
to the good part as soon as possible, pickaxe through these walls.

"The pickaxe welds itself to your hand!"

Oops, the wizard must have cursed it when I wasn't looking.  OK, but I
still have a ring of conflict and a powerful character.  I'll give it a
try anyway, hitting things with my pickaxe and throwing Stormbringer.

Cleaned out the rust monsters and the liches.  Look at the dragons --
"I'm resistant to everything they have, let's chuck this amulet of
reflection and go for life-saving just to be safe".

"The blast of lightning hits you.  Your ring of conflict crumbles into
dust.  Your ring of levitation crumbles into dust."

Well, I cleared out the dragons anyway -- with a pickaxe -- but was
stuck without levitation, and when the wizard reappeared and
surrounded my with minotaurs and such, I eventually succumbed.

I did learn some things out of that game though:

- You can read a scroll of remove curse while blindfolded???  Otherwise
I never would have gotten past the wizard on the castle level on the way
back up.

- Even though Stormbringer doesn't do as much damage as a heavily
enchanted normal weapon, it's worth its weight in gold against the
wizard.  I wouldn't have realized what it does except that I had a
stethoscope I was using on all my opponents.  On a level where you're
prevented from teleporting, but the wizard can still teleport away when
he's in trouble, is there any way to defeat him in straight combat
(ie. no wands) _without_ Stormbringer?

